WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.001 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Last time you were here

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.768 line:92%
we talked about your upbringing.

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
You went to high school with
Slash from Guns N' Roses.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
After you left,

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:08.008
we realized you also went to
high school with Nic Cage.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-That is really impressive.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.679
Did you know each other at all?
-We did.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.648 line:92%
At that time he was Nic Coppola.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Nicolas Coppola.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there was a production
of "Oklahoma"

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was playing
the lead male character.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was in the pit
playing drums.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was the drummer
in the orchestra.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.062 line:92%
And also, Gina Gershon...

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
Another wonderful actress.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...was in the play as well,
playing opposite Nic.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:34.634 line:92%
-And, you know, obviously,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think when we're
all in high school,

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:39.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
the people that are
the theater stars,

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.140 line:92%
you think they're wonderful.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, you were
in a unique position

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.909 line:92%
where they actually were.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.810 line:92%
Could you tell in high school?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you watching them
thinking like,

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.113 line:92%
"Oh, they're gonna be famous?"

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um...I had no idea.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.084 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I had no idea.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.752 line:92%
We're all just doing what we do.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's amazing when
I see them now.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"Wow, we did all right."

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You all did all right.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They have other people wash
their jeans for them,

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that's fine.
It's not a contest.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I want to ask this.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.901 line:92%
You know, when you say --

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:08.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think when
I sit here and I say,

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you went to high school
with all these people,"

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.005
they might think, "Oh, my
God, this must have been --

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
you must have had everything
you could have wanted

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:17.577
to be at a high school --"
but you also had hard jobs.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.679 line:92%
-I left home when I was 15.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you had a job in
high school gutting fish?

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I did.
-So where --

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:28.221 size:84% position:42%
-I worked at a place on
Washington and Rimpau.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was called,
Leroy's Fish Market.

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was one of those,
you know --

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
hood, "you buy, we fry"
fish joints.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:40.633
So yeah, the fish would be
behind the glass counter,

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
and somebody
would come in and say,

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'll have two pounds of this,
five pounds of that."

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd have to then scale it,
cut it,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.776 line:92%
gut it, clean it, and fry it.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-And at the time I used to fry

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.915
mayor Tom Bradley's fish,
cause he would come in.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does anyone remember
Tom Bradley?

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:01.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, there's an airport
named after him.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Um, uh...

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or a terminal at least.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's a terminal,
you're right.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:08.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he used to come in on
Fridays and get his fish.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:09.996 line:92%
I had that job for about a year.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:14.200
So it seems like tonight's whole
theme is about how much I smell.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know, I feel bad.
I feel bad.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:19.272
As you were talking I realized,
"Oh, we've found a theme."

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:23.176
-I smelled for a year and my
mother taught me this trick.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:26.045 size:88% position:44%
She said, "Baby, go home
and bathe with lemons."

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.448
So I would have all of these
lemons at the end of the day

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.249 line:92%
that I'd go get and I'd cut them

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:32.185
and I'd get in the shower
and I'd scrub with lemons.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd still stink.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.788 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I worked at a sub shop

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I just remember
being around onions.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was enough.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.561
So I can only imagine what
it was like cutting a fish.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You came home covered in
fish guts and --.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.598 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, that's not a --
-But it was a great job.

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got to know people
really well.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was one of those
jobs where

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to learn so much
about people.

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you -- I feel like you've
lived in some of the places

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are best in the world
for getting to know

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just people, but uh,
exceptional people.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were in New York and you
lived across the street

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:05.285
when you were a kid -- across
the street from Joe Namath?

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:06.386 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to play catch
with Joe Namath.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where in New York --
Where would you play catch?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.293 line:92%
-I lived at 5 East 82nd Street.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.861 line:92%
He lived at 3 East 82nd street.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:17.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I could see
into his apartment.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.665 line:92%
And, in fact, I didn't --

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:23.203
which was -- in the '70s, Joe
Namath was the man, right?

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.939
-I think it's the apartment most
people would have liked

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:26.706 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to be able to see into.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so I actually
met him again

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.711
several years ago doing
The David Letterman Show.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.814
And I said, "By the way, you
probably don't know who I am."

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "Yeah, I know you."
I said, "No, no.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:39.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was the little kid that
lived across the street

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you used to play
catch with."

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.889
And I said, "I used to look
inside of your apartment."

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:46.259
And he kind of wasn't sure,
and I started telling him

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the things I saw in
the apartment

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:51.531
and the furnishings, and he was
like, "Oh, you did."

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.433 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.968 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah. And um...

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
So yeah, I got to grow up
playing catch with Joe Namath.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.707 size:81% position:41%
-Well, that's not a --
not a bad situation.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.742
-I had a very strange childhood.
-You have, yeah.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say every part
of your life

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.778
has been very interesting,
and that's why it's always

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
lovely to have you here.
Thank you so much.

